sux-ui_preface.sh|177|159|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|A SolidGroundUX application should generally follow these rules:|sux-ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
sux-ui_preface.sh|178|160|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sux-ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
sux-ui_preface.sh|179|161|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|    - Use `say` functions for user-facing status and diagnostic messages.|sux-ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
sux-ui_preface.sh|180|162|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|    - Use rendering helpers for standard titles, sections, labels, and tables.|sux-ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
sux-ui_preface.sh|181|163|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|    - Use prompt and dialog helpers for interactive decisions.|sux-ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
