sux-ui_preface.sh|183|165|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|    - Do not duplicate glyphs or terminal-width calculations locally.|sux-ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
sux-ui_preface.sh|184|166|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|    - Keep machine-readable output separate from styled human-readable output.|sux-ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
sux-ui_preface.sh|185|167|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|    - Respect non-interactive, quiet, debug, and dry-run execution modes.|sux-ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
sux-ui_preface.sh|186|168|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sux-ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
sux-ui_preface.sh|187|169|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Following these conventions gives command-line tools a shared appearance and,|sux-ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
sux-ui_preface.sh|188|170|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|more importantly, shared behavior. Users can learn one interaction model and|sux-ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
sux-ui_preface.sh|189|171|Guidance for Applications|User Interface||normal|||L2Sectionbody|apply it across all SolidGroundUX applications.|sux-ui_preface.sh::User Interface:Guidance for Applications:
