sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|3|1||||normal|||moduleheader|SolidGroundUX - Repair Permissions|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|14|2||||label|||modulebody|Description|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|15|3||||normal|||modulebody|  Reads a pipe-separated permission policy file and applies the declared owner,|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|16|4||||normal|||modulebody|  group, and mode to each target. Relative target paths are resolved below the|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|17|5||||normal|||modulebody|  active SolidGroundUX framework root so the same policy can be used in staged|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|18|6||||normal|||modulebody|  development trees and on installed systems.|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|19|7||||normal|||modulebody||sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|20|8||||normal|||modulebody|  By default a policy row affects only its exact target. An optional filemask extends|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|21|9||||normal|||modulebody|  the rule below a directory: * selects all immediate children, ** selects all|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|22|10||||normal|||modulebody|  descendants recursively, and any other shell-style glob (for example sgnd-*)|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|23|11||||normal|||modulebody|  selects matching immediate children. The declared type still filters directories|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|24|12||||normal|||modulebody|  (d) from regular files (f).|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|25|13||||normal|||modulebody||sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|26|14||||normal|||modulebody|  Exact directory records create the directory when it is missing. File records and|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|27|15||||normal|||modulebody|  masked roots are never invented; missing objects are reported instead.|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|28|16||||normal|||modulebody||sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|29|17||||label|||modulebody|Design principles|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|30|18||||normal|||modulebody|  - Permission policy is declarative and external to the executable.|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|31|19||||normal|||modulebody|  - Permission changes are non-recursive unless a policy row explicitly uses **.|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|32|20||||normal|||modulebody|  - Named filemasks such as sgnd-* are limited to immediate children.|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|33|21||||normal|||modulebody|  - Recursive selection never follows symbolic links outside the declared tree.|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|34|22||||normal|||modulebody|  - The symbolic owner/group value "operator" resolves to the invoking sudo user.|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|35|23||||normal|||modulebody|  - Missing or invalid policy data fails visibly instead of being guessed.|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|36|24||||normal|||modulebody|  - Dry-run reports intended changes without modifying the filesystem.|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|37|25||||normal|||modulebody||sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|38|26||||label|||modulebody|Role in framework|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|39|27||||normal|||modulebody|  - Repairs runtime-writable ownership after root-owned installation or update work.|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|40|28||||normal|||modulebody|  - Provides one reusable implementation for sgnd-setup and Management Console actions.|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|41|29||||normal|||modulebody||sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|42|30||||label|||modulebody|Non-goals|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|43|31||||normal|||modulebody|  - Implicit or unrestricted recursive permission changes.|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|44|32||||normal|||modulebody|  - Following symbolic links while expanding masked selections.|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|45|33||||normal|||modulebody|  - Creating missing regular files or masked search roots.|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|46|34||||normal|||modulebody|  - Inferring ownership or modes that are not declared in the policy file.|sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
sgnd-repair-permissions.sh|47|35||||normal|||modulebody||sgnd-repair-permissions.sh::::
