00-style-default.sh|2|1||||normal|||moduleheader|SolidGroundUX - Default UI Style|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|14|2||||label|||modulebody|Description|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|15|3||||normal|||modulebody|  Provides the default layout and styling rules used by the SolidGroundUX UI layer.|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|16|4||||normal|||modulebody||00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|17|5||||label|||modulebody|The library|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|18|6||||normal|||modulebody|    - Defines spacing, padding, and alignment conventions|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|19|7||||normal|||modulebody|    - Sets default widths for labels and columns|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|20|8||||normal|||modulebody|    - Provides style constants for borders, separators, and layout elements|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|21|9||||normal|||modulebody|    - Complements the color palette with structural presentation rules|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|22|10||||normal|||modulebody|    - Ensures consistent visual composition across all console tools|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|23|11||||normal|||modulebody||00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|24|12||||label|||modulebody|Design principles|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|25|13||||normal|||modulebody|  - Separate layout (style) from color (palette)|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|26|14||||normal|||modulebody|  - Keep styling declarative and easy to override|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|27|15||||normal|||modulebody|  - Favor readability and alignment over compactness|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|28|16||||normal|||modulebody|  - Maintain consistency across all rendered output|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|29|17||||normal|||modulebody||00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|30|18||||label|||modulebody|Role in framework|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|31|19||||normal|||modulebody|  - Structural styling layer used by ui.sh and related modules|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|32|20||||normal|||modulebody|  - Works alongside default-ui-palette.sh to define the full UI theme|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|33|21||||normal|||modulebody|  - Enables consistent layout behavior across scripts and tools|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|34|22||||normal|||modulebody||00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|35|23||||label|||modulebody|Non-goals|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|36|24||||normal|||modulebody|  - Rendering logic or user interaction handling|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|37|25||||normal|||modulebody|  - Terminal capability detection|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|38|26||||normal|||modulebody|  - Dynamic layout adaptation beyond simple width awareness|00-style-default.sh::::
00-style-default.sh|39|27||||normal|||modulebody||00-style-default.sh::::
