sgnd-setup.sh|3|1||||normal|||moduleheader|SolidGroundUX - Setup|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|15|2||||label|||modulebody|Description|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|16|3||||normal|||modulebody|  Provides self-sufficient first-install and lifecycle setup for SolidGroundUX products.|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|17|4||||normal|||modulebody||sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|18|5||||label|||modulebody|The script|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|19|6||||normal|||modulebody|    - Keeps SolidGroundUX release state in the legacy releases/archive locations|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|20|7||||normal|||modulebody|    - Keeps other project release state under /var/lib/solidgroundux/projects/<project>/|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|21|8||||normal|||modulebody|    - Reads release-package.info from incoming ZIPs to select the owning project|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|22|9||||normal|||modulebody|    - Installs a first release by verifying and extracting its complete tar archive|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|23|10||||normal|||modulebody|    - Updates an existing installation and applies the incoming .removed manifest|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|24|11||||normal|||modulebody|    - Rolls back by making the installed filesystem match a selected archived release|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|25|12||||normal|||modulebody|    - Removes the selected project while preserving release packages for later reinstall|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|26|13||||normal|||modulebody|    - Provides root-scoped nuclear cleanup yields for state/log cleanup, code removal,|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|27|14||||normal|||modulebody|      or complete SolidGroundUX eradication without requiring a working framework|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|28|15||||normal|||modulebody|    - Queries GitHub for the latest published release and downloads it only when needed|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|29|16||||normal|||modulebody|    - Bootstraps a clean machine from sgnd-setup.sh plus adjacent product release ZIPs|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|30|17||||normal|||modulebody|    - Installs a canonical setup copy under /var/lib/solidgroundux for future recovery|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|31|18||||normal|||modulebody|    - Uses a small self-contained UI before SolidGroundUX is available|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|32|19||||normal|||modulebody|    - Reuses the normal SolidGroundUX UI primitives/theme when a healthy framework is available|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|33|20||||normal|||modulebody|    - Persists setup parameter values as standalone state|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|34|21||||normal|||modulebody|    - Offers Setup, Management Console, or shell exit after first install|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|35|22||||normal|||modulebody||sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|36|23||||label|||modulebody|Design principles|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|37|24||||normal|||modulebody|  - Standalone operation even when SolidGroundUX is absent or damaged|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|38|25||||normal|||modulebody|  - Product ZIPs are the release unit; acquisition varies, installation does not|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|39|26||||normal|||modulebody|  - Complete release archives; no incremental binary patching|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|40|27||||normal|||modulebody|  - Conservative removal: files/symlinks are removed, directories only when empty|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|41|28||||normal|||modulebody|  - Product ZIP acquisition is transactional; successful installs archive the original ZIP|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|42|29||||normal|||modulebody|  - Bootstrap cleanup is limited to known setup/package files under /tmp|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|43|30||||normal|||modulebody|  - Nuclear cleanup derives its deletion root from the canonical framework-locator algorithm|sgnd-setup.sh::::
sgnd-setup.sh|44|31||||normal|||modulebody||sgnd-setup.sh::::
