sdk-tools_preface.sh|46|27|Creating a New Project|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The workspace generator creates the repository-shaped target-root structure,|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Creating a New Project:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|47|28|Creating a New Project|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|project definitions, optional project MOTD, VS Code workspace file, and a local copy|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Creating a New Project:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|48|29|Creating a New Project|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|of the reusable component templates. It can instantiate starter executable, library,|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Creating a New Project:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|49|30|Creating a New Project|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|and console-module files and can optionally initialize and publish the repository|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Creating a New Project:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|50|31|Creating a New Project|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|through Git/GitHub.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Creating a New Project:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|51|32|Creating a New Project|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Creating a New Project:
