sdk-tools_preface.sh|61|42|Development Phase|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Phase:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|62|43|Development Phase|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The provided templates are intended to be the preferred starting point for new|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Phase:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|63|44|Development Phase|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|components. They contain the recommended metadata headers, bootstrap structure,|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Phase:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|64|45|Development Phase|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|documentation conventions, and coding patterns used throughout the framework.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Phase:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|65|46|Development Phase|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Phase:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|66|47|Development Phase|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Following the templates helps maintain consistency across projects and reduces|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Phase:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|67|48|Development Phase|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|the amount of boilerplate code required.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Phase:
