sdk-tools_preface.sh|154|135|Workspace Layout|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|While individual projects may add folders as needed, the framework expects a|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Workspace Layout:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|155|136|Workspace Layout|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|number of well-known locations. The typical workspace structure mimics the|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Workspace Layout:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|156|137|Workspace Layout|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|expected deployment layout, making it easier to transition from development to|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Workspace Layout:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|157|138|Workspace Layout|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|deployment without reorganizing files.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Workspace Layout:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|158|139|Workspace Layout|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Workspace Layout:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|159|140|Workspace Layout|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|The deployment tools depend on this structure to determine which files to|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Workspace Layout:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|160|141|Workspace Layout|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|include and where to place them during deployment. The structure also helps|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Workspace Layout:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|161|142|Workspace Layout|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|ensure that generated documentation, metadata, and supporting assets are|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Workspace Layout:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|162|143|Workspace Layout|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|maintained consistently across projects.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Workspace Layout:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|163|144|Workspace Layout|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Workspace Layout:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|164|145|Workspace Layout|SDK||emphasis|||L2Sectionbody|Deviate at your own peril.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Workspace Layout:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|165|146|Workspace Layout|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Workspace Layout:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|166|147|Workspace Layout|SDK||highlight|||L2Sectionbody|Images|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Workspace Layout:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|167|148|Workspace Layout|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|  sdk-project-structure.png :: Folder structure of a typical SolidGroundUX project workspace. |sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Workspace Layout:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|168|149|Workspace Layout|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Workspace Layout:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|169|150|Workspace Layout|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Executable applications are typically placed in bin and sbin, reusable|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Workspace Layout:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|170|151|Workspace Layout|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|libraries in lib, and internal implementation helpers in libexec.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Workspace Layout:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|171|152|Workspace Layout|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Workspace Layout:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|172|153|Workspace Layout|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|This separation helps distinguish public interfaces from internal|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Workspace Layout:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|173|154|Workspace Layout|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|implementation details and keeps larger projects maintainable.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Workspace Layout:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|174|155|Workspace Layout|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Workspace Layout:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|175|156|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionheader|Development Conventions|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|176|157|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|177|158|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|SolidGroundUX relies heavily on conventions to keep projects consistent.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|178|159|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|179|160|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Public framework functions should use the sgnd_ prefix.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|180|161|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|181|162|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Framework-public functions use `sgnd_*`. Framework-internal functions shared by|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|182|163|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|cooperating framework libraries use `_sgnd_*`. A plain leading underscore such as|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|183|164|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|`_helper` identifies a script- or module-local private implementation detail. Bash|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|184|165|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|cannot enforce these access levels, but the naming convention communicates intent.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|185|166|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|186|167|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Executable scripts should be based on the executable template.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|187|168|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|User-facing executables should normally be exposed through lightweight wrappers|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|188|169|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|in bin or sbin. The actual implementation script should live in the appropriate|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|189|170|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|product subfolder, usually below libexec, and be invoked by the wrapper.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|190|171|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|191|172|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|This keeps the command path clean while allowing implementation scripts,|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|192|173|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|supporting files, and internal helpers to remain grouped by product.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|193|174|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|194|175|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Reusable libraries should be based on the library template.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|195|176|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|196|177|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Libraries should generally not perform actions merely because they are sourced.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|197|178|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|With the exception of library guards, metadata registration, dependency|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|198|179|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|registration, and similar initialization tasks, sourcing a library should not|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|199|180|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|execute business logic, modify user data, create files, or perform external|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|200|181|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|operations.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|201|182|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|202|183|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Libraries are expected to provide functionality through public functions. The|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|203|184|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|caller decides when that functionality is executed.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|204|185|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|205|186|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Modules intended for menu-driven applications should use the module template.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|206|187|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|207|188|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Metadata headers should be maintained in all framework-managed files.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|208|189|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|209|190|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Documentation should be maintained close to the source code using the framework|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|210|191|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|documentation conventions.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|211|192|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|212|193|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Development-only artifacts should be kept out of the deployed target layout|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|213|194|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|unless they are intentionally part of the product being released.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|214|195|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody||sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|215|196|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|Developers are free to deviate from these conventions when appropriate, but|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|216|197|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|following them generally results in more maintainable projects and more useful|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
sdk-tools_preface.sh|217|198|Development Conventions|SDK||normal|||L2Sectionbody|generated documentation.|sdk-tools_preface.sh::SDK:Development Conventions:
