prepare-release.sh|3|1||||normal|||moduleheader|SolidGroundUX SDK - Prepare Release|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|14|2||||label|||modulebody|Description|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|15|3||||normal|||modulebody|  Provides a release-preparation utility for SolidGroundUX workspaces.|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|16|4||||normal|||modulebody||prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|17|5||||label|||modulebody|The script|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|18|6||||normal|||modulebody|    - Selects target scripts by file or folder|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|19|7||||normal|||modulebody|    - Refreshes version, build, and checksum metadata unless source updates are disabled|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|20|8||||normal|||modulebody|    - Applies optional major or minor version bumps|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|21|9||||normal|||modulebody|    - Supports dry-run verification before committing changes|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|22|10||||normal|||modulebody|    - Ensures release metadata is consistent across processed scripts|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|23|11||||normal|||modulebody|    - Verifies public command wrappers for executable top-level libexec scripts|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|24|12||||normal|||modulebody|    - Creates release tar/manifests/checksums and a complete distributable release ZIP|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|25|13||||normal|||modulebody|    - Copies completed release artifacts directly into a separately selected output directory|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|26|14||||normal|||modulebody|    - Reports the full output paths of product release ZIPs and the optional first-install ZIP|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|27|15||||normal|||modulebody|    - Writes release-package.info at ZIP root so the package identifies its project/release|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|28|16||||normal|||modulebody|    - Uses an explicit removal-baseline manifest from persistent manifest history|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|29|17||||normal|||modulebody|    - Builds a first-install ZIP containing sgnd-setup.sh plus selected product release ZIPs,|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|30|18||||normal|||modulebody|      using the SolidGroundUX/Setup version and the highest build number contained in the package|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|31|19||||normal|||modulebody||prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|32|20||||label|||modulebody|Design principles|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|33|21||||normal|||modulebody|  - Release preparation is deterministic and repeatable|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|34|22||||normal|||modulebody|  - Metadata updates are explicit and convention-based|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|35|23||||normal|||modulebody|  - Safe verification is supported through dry-run mode|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|36|24||||normal|||modulebody|  - Script formatting is preserved when updating field values|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|37|25||||normal|||modulebody||prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|38|26||||label|||modulebody|Role in framework|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|39|27||||normal|||modulebody|  - Pre-release maintenance tool for framework and utility scripts|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|40|28||||normal|||modulebody|  - Ensures release metadata is synchronized before distribution|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|41|29||||normal|||modulebody||prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|42|30||||label|||modulebody|Non-goals|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|43|31||||normal|||modulebody|  - Deploying files to target environments|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|44|32||||normal|||modulebody|  - Managing version control, tagging, or publication workflows|prepare-release.sh::::
prepare-release.sh|45|33||||normal|||modulebody||prepare-release.sh::::
