create-wrappers.sh|14|2||||label|||modulebody|Description|create-wrappers.sh::::
create-wrappers.sh|15|3||||normal|||modulebody|  Creates one or more command wrappers from SolidGroundUX scripts. Source files are|create-wrappers.sh::::
create-wrappers.sh|16|4||||normal|||modulebody|  selected from a source directory using a filename or shell mask. Generated wrappers|create-wrappers.sh::::
create-wrappers.sh|17|5||||normal|||modulebody|  are rendered from the canonical wrapper-template and resolve the active SolidGroundUX|create-wrappers.sh::::
create-wrappers.sh|18|6||||normal|||modulebody|  framework tree from the wrapper path before launching their configured target.|create-wrappers.sh::::
create-wrappers.sh|19|7||||normal|||modulebody||create-wrappers.sh::::
create-wrappers.sh|20|8||||label|||modulebody|Wrapper names|create-wrappers.sh::::
create-wrappers.sh|21|9||||normal|||modulebody|    - Optional Metadata/Wrapper overrides the generated command name.|create-wrappers.sh::::
create-wrappers.sh|22|10||||normal|||modulebody|    - Otherwise script.sh -> sgnd-script and sgnd-script.sh -> sgnd-script.|create-wrappers.sh::::
create-wrappers.sh|23|11||||normal|||modulebody||create-wrappers.sh::::
create-wrappers.sh|24|12||||label|||modulebody|Wrapper target directories|create-wrappers.sh::::
create-wrappers.sh|25|13||||normal|||modulebody|    - <selected-framework-root>/usr/local/bin  (default)|create-wrappers.sh::::
create-wrappers.sh|26|14||||normal|||modulebody|    - <selected-framework-root>/usr/local/sbin|create-wrappers.sh::::
create-wrappers.sh|27|15||||normal|||modulebody||create-wrappers.sh::::
create-wrappers.sh|28|16||||label|||modulebody|Design principles|create-wrappers.sh::::
create-wrappers.sh|29|17||||normal|||modulebody|  - Generated wrappers remain environment-independent.|create-wrappers.sh::::
create-wrappers.sh|30|18||||normal|||modulebody|  - The source directory determines the framework tree that owns the wrappers.|create-wrappers.sh::::
create-wrappers.sh|31|19||||normal|||modulebody|  - Wrapper targets are stored relative to that selected framework root.|create-wrappers.sh::::
create-wrappers.sh|32|20||||normal|||modulebody|  - Wrapper execution follows the active self-locating framework tree.|create-wrappers.sh::::
create-wrappers.sh|33|21||||normal|||modulebody|  - Existing wrappers are not overwritten without confirmation.|create-wrappers.sh::::
create-wrappers.sh|34|22||||normal|||modulebody|  - A filename or mask may select one or multiple source scripts.|create-wrappers.sh::::
create-wrappers.sh|35|23||||normal|||modulebody||create-wrappers.sh::::
